  block (0, 0): 3x4 weights of 32 levels in one plane, 4 partitions (seed 6: the closest to the entries' pattern, 2 texels off it), endpoints 11, 22, 0, 0, 22, 33, 0, 11 (luminance, 24 levels), bytes df db 00 00 41 c0 20 00 f2 46 f2 02 cc c0 ae 03
  decodes to [0, 0.000910580973, 0.00212468882, 0.00303526991, 0.00402471703, 0.00518151652, 0.00604883302, 0.00699541019, 0.00802319311, 0.00913405884, 0.00972121768, 0.0109600937, 0.012286488, 0.0129830325, 0.0137020834, 0.0152085144]
  not exact: the closest block found is within 0.000298 of the table (entry 14: 0.0140000004 as 0.0137020834)
  searched: every block mode the footprint has (a weight grid up to the block, each weight range, one plane), 1 to 4 partitions with the seeds whose partitions are closest to the entries' pattern, the endpoints near each partition's least and greatest entry, the weights by least squares through the infill and then a level at a time; not every encoding, so a closer block may exist where it is not exact.  Every block written is decoded again
  a nearest or filtered read of the texture is that read of the decoded table; no model prices an ASTC read: not measured
